<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Georgievsk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1783">1783</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Georgievsk was signed on 24 July 1783 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erekle-ii">Erekle II</a> of Kartli-Kakheti. Erekle renounced Persian overlordship and accepted a Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> guaranteed his kingdom's territory and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrationi-dynasty">Bagrationi dynasty</a>. Russia failed to defend <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> invaded in 1795, and in 1801 it annexed the kingdom outright.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-georgievsk.jpg" alt="Treaty of Georgievsk" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Treaty_of_Georgievsk_of_1783_(Esadze,_1913).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1783 he signed the <b>Treaty of Georgievsk</b> with Catherine the Great, accepting a Russian protectorate.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-kartli-kakheti">Kingdom of Kartli-Kakheti</a></li></ul></section>
